==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|In fact, calculations suggest only two options: here at Gromas, in the Perkell sector, or here, at Phindar, in the Mandalore sector.|The Mandalore sector's first mention in ''Tarkin'', which incorrectly places Phindar in the sector|<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>}}
The Mandalore sector was first mentioned in ''[[Galaxy Guide 9: Fragments from the Rim]]'', a [[1993]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] supplement written by [[Simon Smith]] and [[Eric S. Trautmann]] for ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]''.<ref name="Fragments from the Rim">''[[Galaxy Guide 9: Fragments from the Rim]]''</ref> It became [[canon]] when it appeared in "[[The Mandalore Plot]]," the twelfth episode of the canon animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''{{'}} [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|second season]].<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" /> It was first canonically identified in the [[2014]] novel [[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']], written by [[James Luceno]]. However, ''Tarkin'' places the [[Phindar system]] in the Mandalore sector,<ref name="Tarkin" /> which conflicted with the system's original Legends placement in the [[Demetras sector]];<ref name="EAOC">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-essential-atlas-online-companion|text=''Star Wars: The Essential Atlas'' Online Companion|int=Star Wars: The Essential Atlas Online Companion}}</ref> as a result, the [[2025]] "[[Star Systems of the Galaxy]]" moved the Phindar system back to the Demetras sector.<ref name="Appendix" />

